{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life","id":671750,"title":"Prometheans and Sedentary Life?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-20T03:12:22-07:00","id":671750,"title":"Prometheans and Sedentary Life?","content":"I were wondering if is possible for a Promethean to have a sedentary life style, and things like a house or a job? There's a way to deal with the side-effects of his own presence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T07:47:46-07:00","id":671903,"title":"","content":"House: rent places by the month. As long as you move at least a mile the wasteland won't become strong enough to be a nuisance.<br /> <br /> Job: Get a solitary job. Night guard, trucker, gravedigger, gardener, etc...<br /> <br /> Disquiet: Unlike what some people think, Disquiet is a long process if your azoth is low. So as long as you don't see someone for more than a couple of scenes every week, you should be fine.<br /> <br /> Wasteland: if the job you get is night guard, the place you work at will become tainted and start deteriorating. It's not a problem if you're a gravedigger, but night guard, stripper or any other job like that will become hard to maintain after a month or two.<br /> <br /> Mitigating these effects: Forge an alchemical pact with other prometheans, learn a few Disquietism transmutations, ask a Quashmal, ask an Awakened, etc...<br /> <br /> My best bet would be that in the Second Edition of Prometheans, these things won't be as hard as they appear in the first edition, so you might be better to wait a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T09:02:03-07:00","id":672055,"title":"","content":"Yeah... looking for a new house every month and changing job every two, is not really what I may call a sedentary life style. As I thought, Promethean is a strictly &quot;on the road&quot; game. I guess it's not a good game for players who enjoy long term plans to gain power and infulence...<br /> <br /> I hope Disquietism and Wasteland will be less oppressive in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 09-20-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T13:18:20-07:00","id":672328,"title":"","content":"I tried that once. And, to my surprise, I was roughly successful for a while. However, all that effort I put in proved to be in vain. <br /> <br /> There are ways to manage Disquiet / Wastelands and have the area be stable... until someone else breezes through town, messes everything up, and sends everything to hell in a handbasket. A firestorm, another promethean, a Centimani, one of the intelligent pandorans (sublimanti, I think?), one of the new alchemists or someone who's tracking down the Divine Fire to make Immortals, Elixers or clones out of your body. And that's not counting the fact that the quashmal exist to push the Created to continue their joint spiritual/physical Pilgrimage (at least from an OOC perspective).<br /> <br /> Sedentary life is only possible if everyone and everything leaves that prommie alone. Because once the ball starts rolling, its nearly impossible to stop without physically removing yourself from the area. So, I'd say its possible to run into an NPC that's like that, but I wouldn't suggest that PCs pull it off for a long term game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:08:19-07:00","id":672391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=671903#post671903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mitigating these effects: Forge an alchemical pact with other prometheans, learn a few Disquietism transmutations, ask a Quashmal, ask an Awakened, etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>That last one would cause more problems than it solves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T17:38:34-07:00","id":672570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=672391#post672391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last one would cause more problems than it solves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and no. It's certainly not a permanent solution, due to Dissonance, and there's the issue of finding them, convincing them to help, and whether they even know <i>how</i> to help. Prometheans are one of the few things that even Mages are unable to really comprehend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T17:55:01-07:00","id":672600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=672055#post672055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... looking for a new house every month and changing job every two, is not really what I may call a sedentary life style. As I thought, Promethean is a strictly &quot;on the road&quot; game. I guess it's not a good game for players who enjoy long term plans to gain power and infulence...<br /> <br /> I hope Disquietism and Wasteland will be less oppressive in second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Promethean is not Vampire or Mage. The game stays in the first tier of power forever (second, if you're really into that). Also, say you get a job as a gardener working all around town, you won't have to find a new job for a while. As for finding new living spaces, well... I don't know about you but a single mile does not mean the next town. It simply means you'll probably need a car. Heck you could even live in an old wolksvagen, cycling the local wall-marts. Get yourself a storage room somewhere to stock the important stuff and live in your car. It would still be a game focused in a single city rather than a string of cities across the state.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have too high hopes for long-term influence building in second edition. Promethean is a game of philosophy and humanism, not of power-struggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:33:46-07:00","id":673077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=672570#post672570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and no. It's certainly not a permanent solution, due to Dissonance, and there's the issue of finding them, convincing them to help, and whether they even know <i>how</i> to help. Prometheans are one of the few things that even Mages are unable to really comprehend.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's lots of things that Mages are unable to comprehend - pretty much everything supernatural in the Fallen World beyond ghosts, goetics and spirits. And mages generally still suffer from Disquiet. Even if the ST allows them to use Mind 4 to &quot;cure&quot; it, its easy to slip up and forget to cast the spell, and then turn on the prommie.<br /> <br /> Promethean is a game about being an outcast. Building up long lasting human friends without achieving the New Dawn is something rare and special, because its borderline impossible. Having an Awakened associate has a very good chance of backfiring on you. Only spiritual beings like ghosts, spirits and goetics are immune; demons also might be immune, considering they're very much not human either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=672600#post672600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean is not Vampire or Mage. The game stays in the first tier of power forever (second, if you're really into that). Also, say you get a job as a gardener working all around town, you won't have to find a new job for a while. As for finding new living spaces, well... I don't know about you but a single mile does not mean the next town. It simply means you'll probably need a car. Heck you could even live in an old wolksvagen, cycling the local wall-marts. Get yourself a storage room somewhere to stock the important stuff and live in your car. It would still be a game focused in a single city rather than a string of cities across the state.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't have too high hopes for long-term influence building in second edition. Promethean is a game of philosophy and humanism, not of power-struggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're going to talk about tiers, prommies are firmly stuck in tier 1. A large enough group of Created where they could have a city-based society would definitely destroy said city with Wastelands and Disquiet. Just too much compounding it. Like I said above, a single prommie can hang out in the city if nothing goes wrong. Its everybody else that will send things to hell and back. And how often, as a PC, do you get left alone?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T05:53:41-07:00","id":673091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=673077#post673077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's lots of things that Mages are unable to comprehend - pretty much everything supernatural in the Fallen World beyond ghosts, goetics and spirits. And mages generally still suffer from Disquiet. Even if the ST allows them to use Mind 4 to &quot;cure&quot; it, its easy to slip up and forget to cast the spell, and then turn on the prommie.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one of the cases.<br /> <br /> However, the best case situation for the Prommie is to have the Awakened point the way to milestones to the Prommie from Fate but that may decrease the value of them.<br /> <br /> It would be more accurate that an Awakened may attempt to do the thing for the Prommie which ends up getting screwed up in the process.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T08:23:25-07:00","id":673191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/671750-prometheans-and-sedentary-life?p=672600#post672600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for finding new living spaces, well... I don't know about you but a single mile does not mean the next town. It simply means you'll probably need a car. Heck you could even live in an old wolksvagen, cycling the local wall-marts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pick two places just over a mile apart. So long as you visit both of them every day, you can avoid a Wasteland building up - and there's no reason one can't be where you live. The Wasteland isn't hard to prevent, it's just that preventing it is <i>constant</i>. And of course there's what [b]MCN[/I] said about someone else coming through town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}